# Intro
A reproduction of Smith et al. 2021 (MNRAS 506, 3882), Figure 2: four
co-located ionizing sources in a uniform 100 cm^-3 background, with a
10 pc-radius, 1e4 cm^-3 clump centered 20 pc away along +x (HEALPix
nside=1 pixel 4's center direction). Each source is 19.2 Msun
(Q_H ~ 2.5e48 s^-1), matching the paper's 4 sources totalling
Q_H ~ 1e49 s^-1.

See `../StromgrenSphereClump/` for the sibling example that instead
calibrates clump placement against this code's own measured ionization
front reach -- useful for testing the angular budget-splitting
mechanism in isolation, rather than reproducing this paper's absolute
scale.

## Metallicity
`initial_metallicity=0` (pure hydrogen, matching the paper) is the
default. This code's own ionized-gas temperature floor is
metallicity-dependent, reaching ~47,500 K at Z=0, not the paper's flat
1e4 K -- so `r_HII` runs systematically larger than the paper's own
numbers. The validated erosion-matrix results use `initial_metallicity=0`
combined with the `IONIZATION_FEEDBACK_DEBUG_FIXED_IONIZED_TEMPERATURE_K=1e4`
build flag (see Configure above) to match the paper's 1e4 K convention
instead. `initial_metallicity=0.231 ./run.sh` (the Z/Zsun that gives
T_collisional=1e4 K exactly) is an alternative, untested by the erosion
matrix, that reaches the same T_i without the build flag.

## Resolution
Gas particle mass defaults to 20 Msun, matching Smith et al. 2021's own
resolution (~175k particles total). Hu et al. 2017's convergence-test
levels (4, 0.5, 0.0625, 0.0078125 Msun) are also available via
`gas_mass=X ./run.sh`; particle count scales as 1/gas_mass.

## Temperature IC
The diffuse background and clump are set to different temperatures in
pressure equilibrium (n*T equal on both sides) by `makeIC_clump.py`'s
`--temperature` (background 1000 K by default). `SPH:initial_temperature: 0`
in params.yml is required for this -- otherwise it overwrites the
per-particle IC values.

`rebuild_time_myr`, `deterministic`, `nside`, `initial_metallicity`,
`gas_mass`, and `density_factor` are all overridable via env var (see
run.sh). `density_factor=1 ./run.sh` degenerates the clump to the
background density, reproducing the paper's own no-clump reference
test.

## Cadence
`GEARFeedback:HII_rebuild_time_Myr=0.01` (fixed, unchanged by Phase 4b) is
a numerical parameter, not a physical one -- verified cadence-independent by the 6-point sweep in
`theory/GEAR/Radiation/04_validation.tex` -- and may be changed freely.

# Configure
Validated configuration (matches the papers' `T_i=1e4 K` convention):
```
./configure --disable-mpi --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle --with-chealpix=path/to/chealpix CFLAGS="-DIONIZATION_FEEDBACK_DEBUG_FIXED_IONIZED_TEMPERATURE_K=1e4"
make -j
```
`--with-chealpix` is required for `nside=1`; `nside=0` works without it.

# Run
`nside=0 ./run.sh` and `nside=1 ./run.sh` (use `run_name=nside0 ./run.sh`
/ `run_name=nside1 ./run.sh` to keep both outputs) run the geometry
from Figure 2, reproducing the top (spherical) and bottom (HEALPix)
panels respectively.

`run.sh` runs `plot_temperature_hii.py` on the run's own final
snapshot automatically (`run_analysis=1` by default; set
`run_analysis=0` to skip). It prints `r_HII`/`r_physics` and writes
`temperature_{projection,slice}_<snapshot>.png` next to the run's
output.

# Measuring clump erosion
Identify clump-member particles once, by particle ID, at
`snapshot_0000` (position within `clump_radius_pc` of the clump
centre, density above the clump's own IC threshold), then track the
same IDs to the final snapshot -- not a fresh position-based
selection, since the clump drifts.
```
python3 clump_erosion_matrix.py            # total mass remaining, bar chart
python3 clump_hemisphere_erosion.py        # near (star-facing) vs. far split + mass-conservation check
python3 clump_hemisphere_density_change.py # near vs. far median n_H, final/t=0 (continuous, not threshold-based)
```
All three take `--gas-mass`/`--metallicity`/`--rebuild` to select a
subset of a matrix of runs (see `--help`); run directories are
expected to be named
`gas${gas_mass}_z${z_label}_nside${nside}_rebuild${rebuild_time_myr}`.
